@startuml uc-016-place-travel-order
title UC-016 Place a Travel Order — UX task flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  BorderColor #333333
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4CC
  DiamondBorderColor #8A6D1D
}

|ACT-001 Customer|
start
:MSS 1 — Submit accepted Sales Offer\nfor order placement;

|System|
:MSS 2 — Retrieve confirmed context\nand check authorization;
:MSS 3 — Obtain and validate\nmandatory information;
if (Context, authority, and\ninformation sufficient?) then (yes)
else (no — EXT 2-3)
  :Identify what is needed;
  :Preserve the last confirmed state\nand acceptance evidence;
  :Communicate the missing need\nwithout creating an order;
  stop
endif

:MSS 4 — Perform Sales responsibilities\nfor order placement;
if (Same accepted offer already\nproduced a Travel Order?) then (yes — acceptance example)
  :Return the same identifiable Travel Order;
else (no)
  :Coordinate required responsibilities;
  if (Responsibilities completed?) then (yes)
    :Create exactly one identifiable Travel Order;
  else (no — EXT 4)
    :Record the partial or uncertain result;
    :Avoid presenting success or\ncreating a duplicate order;
    :Offer retry, revision, or\nhuman-assistance path;
    stop
  endif
endif

|ACT-001 Customer|
:MSS 5 — Review or confirm\nthe resulting state;
if (Result confirmed?) then (yes)
else (no — EXT 5)
  |System|
  :Preserve the confirmed baseline\nand acceptance evidence;
  :Return affected information\nfor revision;
  stop
endif

|System|
:MSS 6 — Record outcome, provenance,\nand unresolved next steps;
:Communicate the Travel Order\nand next steps to affected actors;
stop

legend bottom
Textual UC-016 is authoritative.
MSS = main success scenario; EXT = extension.
endlegend
@enduml
